From: Antigravity AI Team <dev@antigravity.ai>
Subject: [PATCH 0002/0003] arm64: dts: s905w: configure GPIODV_24 (GPIO 474) for STV3000 standby LED

Configure GPIODV_24 (GPIO 474) active-low polarity for STV3000 bicolor LED:
- Active Low (0) = Red LED ON (Standby Mode)
- Active High (1) = Red LED OFF / Blue LED Active (Normal Operation)

Signed-off-by: Antigravity AI Team <dev@antigravity.ai>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-gxl-s905w-stv3000.dts | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-gxl-s905w-stv3000.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-gxl-s905w-stv3000.dts
index d5e6f78..f8e9a1b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-gxl-s905w-stv3000.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-gxl-s905w-stv3000.dts
@@ -112,6 +112,12 @@
 	sysled: sysled {
 		status = "okay";
 		compatible = "amlogic,led-sys";
+		led_gpio = <&gpio GPIODV_24 0>; /* Active Low = Red Standby */
 	};
 };
-- 
